# vault — Your Brain

This is the vault. Write notes here. This is not the tooling repo.

The tooling repo is at `../` (pbrain root). Scripts and slash commands live there. Write code there, not here.

Use Obsidian to browse and edit notes. This vault is plain markdown — every file is readable and editable in any text editor.

---

## Where each kind of note lives

| Content | Directory |
|---|---|
| Daily notes | `agent-work/daily/YYYY-MM-DD.md` |
| Ideas in progress | `agent-work/ideas/` |
| Compiled concept pages | `agent-work/concepts/` |
| Source notes (books, papers, links) | `agent-work/sources/` |
| People pages | `agent-work/people/` |
| Saved AI conversations | `agent-work/chat-history/` |
| Archived drafts | `agent-work/archive/` |
| Historical Notion export (read-only) | `notion-mirror/` |

---

## Frontmatter schema

Every `agent-work/` note gets a frontmatter block. Required fields:

```yaml
---
type: idea           # idea | concept | source | person | daily | chat | project
title: "Human-readable title"
tags: []
created: YYYY-MM-DD
---
```

Optional fields by type:

**idea:**
```yaml
status: draft        # draft | developing | archived
```

**concept:**
```yaml
status: living       # living | archived
related: []          # list of [[slug]] references
```

**source:**
```yaml
source_url: ""
author: ""
status: draft        # draft | processed | archived
```

**person:**
```yaml
related: []
```

**daily:** (no optional fields beyond the required set)

---

## Wikilink convention

Use `[[slug]]` to reference other notes. The slug is the filename without `.md`.

Examples:
- `[[my-idea-slug]]`
- `[[concept-name]]`
- `[[2026-01-15]]` (daily note)

gbrain builds an entity graph from these links. Use them freely — they're how the graph gets populated.

