## Available slash commands

All commands are defined in `../.claude/commands/` and are available here too.

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `/journal` | Create or open today's daily note. |
| `/brainstorm <topic>` | Create a brainstorming file in `ideas/`. |

---

## Writing voice

Direct. First-person. Present tense. Compressed — no filler words.

- "I think X" not "One might consider X"
- "X works because Y" not "It is worth noting that X may work due to Y"
- State the claim first, evidence second
- Compiled truth on top of a concept page; timeline of how thinking evolved at the bottom

---

## gbrain notes

gbrain indexes everything under `vault/`. It auto-creates entity pages in `agent-work/people/` and `agent-work/concepts/` when references accumulate.

Do not edit gbrain-generated pages without understanding they may be regenerated. Add a `<!-- manual -->` comment at the top if you want to signal it's been curated.

The gbrain index lives in `.gbrain/` (gitignored). Run `gbrain sync` to update it after adding new notes.
